# UX / Friction Rules — The Conversion Engineer

Read `00-brand-core.mdc`, `02-conversion-funnel.mdc`, and `06-web-platform-architecture.mdc` first.

## Mobile-first, always

Traffic arrives from Instagram and YouTube — assume a phone, assume a fast thumb, assume low
patience. Any layout decision gets tested at mobile width first, not as an afterthought.

## Load speed is a conversion feature

Cold social traffic bounces within seconds if the page stalls. Treat load time as part of the
"Effort & Sacrifice" side of the value equation.

**Next.js homepage pattern (required):**
- Hero + letter: eager load
- All other homepage sections: `LazySection` + `next/dynamic` — do not revert to monolithic imports
- Hero video: `preload="metadata"`, poster frame, no blocking below-fold JS

## The apply form (`/apply`)

- **Engagement Readiness Application** — server action to Nest `POST /intake/applications`
- Minimum viable fields only. Every extra field is friction the funnel can't afford.
- Immediate confirmation on submit — no dead air after POST.
- **No login, no OAuth, no account creation** before or during apply. Applicants are public.
- Do not embed the legacy homepage `apply-form` or WhatsApp-only free-slot flow.

## Operator UX (`/sign-in`, `/review`)

- Separate from applicant flow. OAuth via Nest; token in localStorage; list at `/review`.
- After OAuth callback, land on `/review` — never `/apply`.
- Review UI is utilitarian; brand voice applies lightly. Clarity over persuasion.

## Navigation discipline

- Primary applicant CTAs: `/work-with-us` and `/apply` — not `#apply`, not homepage hash anchors
  as the main conversion path.
- No competing exits near the last-call section. Dual CTA (read + apply) is the exception —
  both serve the same commitment ramp.
- Popups/modals are earned, not default. Nothing interrupts before the letter (agitation rung).

## Testing discipline

Any UX change that touches apply flow, auth boundaries, or CTA copy should note which funnel rung
it affects and what it moves (click-through, form starts, form completions, reviewer load time).

Run the **`ux-onboarding-flow`** skill (walk + `scripts/run-flow-checks.mjs`) before shipping
onboarding or review UI changes. Log outcomes to `.cursor/skills/ux-onboarding-flow/ROLLOUT.yaml`.
